  ('2d70f877-62a7-52d1-89c1-208708b5ad11', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '绝对明确 2. 相对明确 作用 修饰限定先行词，不能省 略，影响表意 补充说明先行词，可以省 略，不影响 非限制性定语从句总结 6', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 5, true, 42, null),
  ('6bf4fa30-27eb-5070-90ec-8e380f3d0cf0', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.【绝对明确】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 43, null),
  ('6b9a9709-1570-5323-8d6f-34129fbf39f2', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'but two years ago Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have any physical product at all.【绝对明确】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 44, null),
  ('92bc6616-3849-532c-95cf-663ea7e7ca80', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. 【相对明确-短期投资者】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 45, null),
  ('f1e6c7eb-0b93-5e4d-8bc0-4f4ae9941041', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'they''ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges. 【相对明确-学费】 非限制性定语从句阅读方式-分清主从句，意群，谁跟谁并列 7 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers. 在爱荷华州，这一表态并未得到广泛认同。该州田野上风力发电机星罗棋布，风电已占全州发电量的 36%。科技巨头（如微软）正因清洁能源的充沛供应而纷纷选址于此，为其数据中心提供动力支持。 第一步：找出所有动词 did not play，dot，provide，are being attracted， to power 第二步：非谓语动词词组=起点+终点（前） 起点：to do；doing；done 终点=下一个标点符号前；下一个连接词前；下一 个动词前 to power their data centers. 第三步：一个连词+搭配一个动词+终点（下一个 标点符号；下一个连接词；下一个动词）', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 46, null),
  ('f7240de3-7d59-5155-9ff9-180cbe137c6e', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where wind turbines .... electricity generation', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 7, true, 47, null),
  ('ec603ac7-1d79-5b32-a631-fcff090e620b', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where tech giants.... clean energy 解决三个问题①形式中判断是非限制性定从 ②分清楚句子层次，主 从句，谁跟谁并列③复现意群 ④学有余力者，翻译 8 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 问题一：复现意群？？？ 上下义复现【概括+具体】：2组词 同义复现/替换：1组词 指代复现：1组 非限制性定从，大于8个字，所以翻译时候独立成句 9 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 上下义复现【概括+具体】：clean energy-wind；tech giants-Microsoft 同义复现/替换：provide electricity=to power 指代复现： tech giants-their 翻译：非限制性定从，大于8个字，所以翻译时候独立成句 10 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 但这一说法在爱荷华州并不受许多民众认可。在该州，风力发电机遍布田野，风能供应全州 36% 的 发电量；也正是在该州，充足的清洁能源吸引了微软这类科技巨头入驻，为它们的数据中心供 电。 真题演练六：风能供电，为科技巨头数据中心供电，与这个方向更 贴近 11 President Trump has underlined fossil fuels——especially coal——as the path to economic growth. In a recent speech in Iowa，he dismissed wind power as an unreliable energy source. But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 7, true, 48, null),
  ('d7f47969-3e9c-53f9-bc8c-98a185d25be2', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'It can be learned that in Iowa，_____. [A] wind is a widely used energy source风能是一种被广泛使用的能源 [B] wind energy has replaced fossil fuels风能已经取代了化石燃料 [C] tech giants are investing in clean energy科技巨头正在投资清洁能源 [D] there is a shortage of clean energy supply清洁能源供应存在短缺 12', null, 'A', '选项A正确。原文明确提到爱荷华州“风力发电机星罗棋布”（wind turbines dot the fields），且风
电占全州发电量的36%（provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation），说明风能已被广泛利
用。
选项B错误。文中未提及风能“完全取代”化石燃料（replaced fossil fuels），仅强调其占比高，且特朗普
仍主张发展化石燃料。
选项C片面。科技巨头（如微软）因清洁能源可用性被吸引（attracted by clean energy），但“投资清洁
能源”这一主动行为未被明确说明。
选项D与原文矛盾。文中指出清洁能源充足（availability of clean energy），而非短缺。
方法二：非限制性定语从句中找复现词wind，复现词是重点讨论对象，所以更有可能放在选项的主语位
置，排除CD，句子不是讨论tech giants，也不是a shortage of clean energy supply，然后B有fossil
fuel非限制性定从里没有这个意群的重现。
真题演练七
13
①The power and ambition of the giants of the digital economy is astonishing - Amazon has just
announced the purchase of the upmarket grocery chain Whole Foods for $13.5bn, but two years ago
Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have
any physical product at all. ②What WhatsApp offered Facebook was an intricate and finely detailed
web of its users'' friendships and social lives.
According to Paragraph 1, Facebook acquired WhatsApp for its____.
A. digital products数字产品
B. user information用户信息
C. physical assets实体资产
D. quality service优质服务
答案及解析
14
正确答案：B（user information）
选项B正确。原文明确提到，WhatsApp为Facebook提供的是“用户友谊和社交生活的复杂而
精细的网络”（an intricate and finely detailed web of its users'' friendships and social lives），这属
于用户信息范畴。选项A（digital products）错误。WhatsApp本身是数字服务，但收购原因并非其
“产品”，而是用户数据。选项C（physical assets）错误。文中强调WhatsApp“没有任何实体产品”
（doesn''t have any physical product at all）。选项D（quality service）错误。服务质量未被提及，
收购核心是用户社交关系数据。
真题演练八
15
Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to
invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. This has been dubbed “quarterly capitalism.”', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 11, true, 49, null),
  ('738ce58a-4bca-5280-b52a-040009824d6d', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'It is argued that the influence of transient investment on public companies can be ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "indirect间接的；迂回的；非直接的"}, {"key": "B", "text": "adverse不利的；负面的；有害的；"}, {"key": "C", "text": "minimal极小的；最低限度的；微不足道的"}, {"key": "D", "text": "temporary暂时的；临时的 universe n.宇宙 ad朝向"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '原文指出，短期投资者（transient investors）要求公司实现高额季度利润，这会阻碍企业对长期研
究或培养客户忠诚度的投入，这种现象被称为“季度资本主义”（quarterly capitalism）。关键动词“hinder”
（阻碍）直接表明短期投资的影响是负面的，与选项B“adverse”（不利的）完全对应。
其他选项分析：A项“indirect”（间接的）：未提及间接影响，原文是直接阻碍。C项“minimal”（微小的）：
与“hinder”的负面程度矛盾。D项“temporary”（暂时的）：短期投资者的行为可能导致长期负面影响，不符
合“temporary”的短暂性。
真题演练九
17
①That said, there is a way in which grade forgiveness satisfies colleges’ own needs as well.
②For public institutions, state funds are sometimes tied partly to their success on metrics such
as graduation rates and student retention—so better grades can, by boosting figures like those, mean
more money. ③And anything that raises GPAs will likely make students—who, at the end of the day,
are paying the bill—feel they’ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another
big concern for colleges.', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 15, false, 50, null),
  ('2975e136-c2a0-5d0f-abf4-b6ce1682c893', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to', '[{"key": "A", "text": "obtain more financial support 获取更多财政资金支持 / 拿到更多经费补贴"}, {"key": "B", "text": "boost their student enrollments促进招生"}, {"key": "C", "text": "improve their teaching quality 提升教学质量"}, {"key": "D", "text": "meet local governments'' needs 满足地方政府的需求"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 17, true, 51, null),
  ('11da5c03-fa7c-585c-a852-f6bcfe9d006a', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to A. obtain more financial support ✅（正确答案）', null, '', '原文第5段指出，公立大学的州政府拨款部分取决于毕业率和学生留存率等指标，而“grade forgiveness”通过
提高GPA间接提升了这些数据，从而帮助学校获得更多财政支持。
B. boost their student enrollments B 混淆留存率 retention 和招生率 enrollments，偷换概念；
C. improve their teaching quality（与教学质量无关，无中生有）
D. meet local governments'' needs（词义偷换：把政府考核要求篡改为政府自身需求（needs），原文无依据；
推导过远：属于多层间接推论，不是政策直接带来的结果；
片面狭隘：只能勉强贴合半句内容，无法完整对应段落里高校的两大收益点，偏离段落总起句 “满足高校自
身需求” 的核心。）
