②For public institutions, state funds are sometimes tied partly to their success on metrics such
as graduation rates and student retention—so better grades can, by boosting figures like those, mean
more money. ③And anything that raises GPAs will likely make students—who, at the end of the day,
are paying the bill—feel they’ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another
big concern for colleges.', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 15, false, 72, null),
  ('fdc88ab7-635d-5157-a21b-8f35745c4fe1', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to', '[{"key": "A", "text": "obtain more financial support 获取更多财政资金支持 / 拿到更多经费补贴"}, {"key": "B", "text": "boost their student enrollments促进招生"}, {"key": "C", "text": "improve their teaching quality 提升教学质量"}, {"key": "D", "text": "meet local governments'' needs 满足地方政府的需求"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 17, true, 73, null),
  ('5e415db9-72e5-566f-ba7e-fcde46804366', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to A. obtain more financial support ✅（正确答案）', null, '', '原文第5段指出，公立大学的州政府拨款部分取决于毕业率和学生留存率等指标，而“grade forgiveness”通过
提高GPA间接提升了这些数据，从而帮助学校获得更多财政支持。
B. boost their student enrollments B 混淆留存率 retention 和招生率 enrollments，偷换概念；
C. improve their teaching quality（与教学质量无关，无中生有）
D. meet local governments'' needs（词义偷换：把政府考核要求篡改为政府自身需求（needs），原文无依据；
推导过远：属于多层间接推论，不是政策直接带来的结果；
片面狭隘：只能勉强贴合半句内容，无法完整对应段落里高校的两大收益点，偏离段落总起句 “满足高校自
身需求” 的核心。）
