  ('73b7e2e4-b20c-5f58-b069-f3c90764568d', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'that it is.....not the mere possession of bits, 相当于it is A not B', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 35, true, 181, null),
  ('85d90329-de00-506e-b85a-56e6c823f062', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'that gives the data value. 强调句补充二; 结论：强调部分一般会成为考点 36 But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value. 作用：通过调整句子结构或使用特定词汇，突出句子中的某个部分，使其更引人注意。 用 It is/was + 强调部分 + that/who + 句子剩余部分 特点：强调主语、宾语、状语等成分（不能强调谓语动词）。人用 who/that，物/时间/地点等用 that。 例子：原句：Tom broke the vase yesterday.（汤姆昨天打碎了花瓶。） 强调主语：It was Tom who/that broke the vase yesterday.（是汤姆昨天打碎了花瓶。） 强调宾语：It was the vase that Tom broke yesterday.（汤姆昨天打碎的是花瓶。） 强调时间：It was yesterday that Tom broke the vase.（是昨天汤姆打碎了花瓶。） 如何判断是强调结构：去掉强调结构，不影响句子完整性 not the mere possession of bits（插入语用作对比） 真题演练一 37 DeepMind has almost apologised. The NHS trust has mended its ways. Further arrangements—and there may be many—between the NHS and DeepMind will be carefully scrutinised to ensure that all necessary permissions have been asked of patients and all unnecessary data has been cleaned. There are lessons about informed patient consent to learn. But privacy is not the only angle in this case and not even the most important. Ms Denham chose to concentrate the blame on the NHS trust, since under existing law it "controlled" the data and DeepMind merely "processed" it. But this distinction misses the point that it is processing and aggregation, not the mere possession of bits, that gives the data value. The author argues in Paragraph 2 that ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "privacy protection must be secured at all costs必须不惜一切代价保护隐私"}, {"key": "B", "text": "leaking patients'' data is worse than selling it泄露患者数据比售卖患者数据性质更恶劣"}, {"key": "C", "text": "making profits from patients'' data is illegal利用患者数据牟利属于违法行为"}, {"key": "D", "text": "the value of data comes from the processing of it数据的价值来源于对数据的加工处理 C为什么不选:C. making profits from patients'' data is illegal利用 患者数据牟利属于违法行为"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 35, false, 182, null),
  ('d30584ca-4099-52f6-9c55-46042fe14d68', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The authors of the paper believe that first-generation students____ . [A]may lack opportunities to apply for research projects可能缺少申报科研项目的机会 [B]are inexperienced in handling their issues at college在大学里处理自身问题缺乏经验 [C]can have a potential influence on other students可能会对其他学生产生潜在影响 [D]are actually indifferent to the achievement gap实际上对学业成绩差距漠不关心 41', null, '及解析', '', '英语2/长难句3-主表同从.pdf', 40, true, 183, null),
  ('1cb87f25-4cd4-5c52-93ee-5861d0ebff7d', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', '：ACD 错在哪里 定位关键句："first-generation students may be most lacking not in potential but in practical knowledge about how to deal with the issues that face most college students" ❌ [A] may lack opportunities to apply for research projects 错因：无中生有 + 偷换概念 原文说的是缺乏 practical knowledge about how to deal with issues（处理问题的实践知识） A 选项把它偷换成了 opportunities to apply for research projects（申请研究项目的机会） research projects 这个概念在原文中根本不存在 出题人埋坑：利用"大学生"背景，诱导你联想到"科研项目"，但原文讨论的是"practical knowledge"（实践知识），而非 "opportunities"（机会）。 ❌ [C] can have a potential influence on other students 错因：曲解原文词汇 原文的 potential 是指"潜力、潜能"，用于说明第一代大学生不是没有潜力 C 选项把 potential 曲解成了"潜在的"（potential as an adjective），然后造出"对其他学生有潜在影响"这个意思 出题人埋坑：利用同一个词的不同词性和含义制造干扰，考生看到"potential"就以为对上了，实际上完全偏离原意。 [D] are actually indifferent to the achievement gap 错因：无中生有 + 相反方向原文说 "close the achievement gap"（缩小成绩差距），这是研究者想要达成的目标 第一代大学生是受害者/对象（他们的成绩差距需要被缩小），而不是对这个问题漠不关心的人 indifferent（漠不关心）这个态度在原文中完全没有依据 出题人埋坑：利用"achievement gap"这个原文词汇，但给它强加了"漠不关心"的负面态度，属于典型的"用原文词包装 错误意思"。 真题演练三 42 自然段一： ①Americans should take steps to protect their digital privacy. ②Despite the fact that keeping sensitive information on devices such as phones is increasingly a requirement of normal life，citizens still have a right to expect private documents to remain private and protected by the Constitution’s prohibition on unreasonable searches. In Paragraphs 1，the author shows his concern that ______.', '[{"key": "A", "text": "principles are hard to be clearly expressed各项准则难以清晰阐明"}, {"key": "B", "text": "the court is giving police less room for action法院留给警方的操作空间正在缩小"}, {"key": "C", "text": "citizens’ privacy is not effectively protected公民的隐私未能得到有效保护"}, {"key": "D", "text": "phones are used to store sensitive information手机被用来储存敏感信息"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '原文重点：作者提到，尽管在数字设备上存储敏感信息已成为现代生活的常态，但公民仍有权期望
私人文件受到保护，并受到宪法禁止不合理搜查的保障。这暗示当前公民的隐私可能未得到充分保护。
选项分析：A项“原则难以明确表达”未提及。B项“法院给警察的行动空间更小”与段落无关。C项“公民隐私
未得到有效保护”与作者担忧一致。D项“手机用于存储敏感信息”是事实陈述，但非作者主要关切。排除法：
D是现象描述，而C是作者的核心观点，因此选C。
